@start
set-bg: img/map_2.jpg
new-page: true

= Social Democracy Redux: The Two SPDs (An Alternate History)

> *"It is difficult for those who have not experienced the 'Age of Catastrophe' of the twentieth century in central Europe to see what it meant to live in a world that was simply not expected to last, in something that could not really even be described as a world, but merely as a provisional way-station between a dead past and a future not yet born, unless perhaps in the depth of revolutionary Russia. Nowhere was this more palpable than in the dying days of the Weimar Republic."*

 - Eric Hobsbawm, Interesting Times (2002)

<img src="img/reichstag_2.jpg" alt="The Reichstag building">

This is a game of alternate history. While historical accuracy is a major concern, keep in mind that this is a *game* and an alternate history, and that any divergence from actual events will necessarily have to involve some element of make-believe. Nevertheless, please let the author know if there are any glaring mistakes.

For more information on the politics and government of the German Republic, see the "Library" page on the top left. If this is your first time playing the game, it is strongly recommended that you read at least some of this information.

Please select your desired start date.

- @1925_start: 1925: The Death of Ebert - Recommended
- @1928_start: 1928: The Age of Catastrophe
- @1930_start: 1930: In This Historic Hour
- @settings: Settings.

@1925_start
go-to: 1925_root
new-page: true

= 1925: The Death of Ebert

*"You will understand and know the German Republic better when it elects Hindenburg president."*
- Jacques Bainville, November 1918

<img src="img/hindenburg_election.jpg" alt="A Hindenburg Election Poster">

It is an uncertain time for German democracy. Though the crises of 1923 have subsided and given way to a stabilization and normalization, the bourgeois parties continue to shift to the right to exclude us from government, even including the anticonstitutional DNVP in the form of the Luther cabinet which has just assumed power.

The task of Social Democracy is to prepare itself so that when the government inevitably falls due to disagreements between the left and right of the bourgeois parties, we will be seen by the workers of Germany a viable alternative.

Please select your desired difficulty to begin.

- @1925_easy: Begin (Easy Difficulty)
- @1925_main: Begin (Normal Difficulty)
- @1925_hard: Begin (Normal Difficulty)
- @1925_historical: Begin (Historical Mode)
- @1928_start: Change to 1928 Start Date
- @1930_start: Change to 1930 Start Date
- @settings: Settings.

@1928_start
go-to: 1928_root
new-page: true

= 1928: The Age of Catastrophe

*"The Weimar Constitution is not a socialist constitution. But we stand by the principles enshrined in it—the principles of a state based on the rule of law, of equal rights, of social justice. In this historic hour, we German Social Democrats solemnly pledge ourselves to the principles of humanity and justice, of freedom and socialism. No Enabling Act gives you the power to destroy ideas that are eternal and indestructible."
- Otto Wels, Speech Against the Passage of the Enabling Act, 1933

<img src="img/bankrun.jpg" alt="A Bankrun">

It is a bright time for German democracy. After a period of struggle, inflation is finally under control, and the economy is expanding steadily. In foreign policy, we have reached agreements with the Western powers and the Soviet Union that might make genuine peace a reality.

Now, the task of Social Democracy is to prepare for the next election. The bourgeois-right government of Wilhelm Marx is unpopular, and we stand to gain. Perhaps the next government will have a socialist majority.

Please select your desired difficulty to begin.

- @1928_easy: Begin (easy difficulty)
- @1928_main: Begin (normal difficulty)
- @1928_hard: Begin (hard difficulty)
- @1928_historical: Begin (historical mode)
- @1925_start: Change to 1925 Start Date
- @1930_start: Change to 1930 Start Date
- @settings: Settings.

@1930_start
go-to: 1930_root
new-page: true

= 1930: In This Historic Hour

*"The Weimar Constitution is not a socialist constitution. But we stand by the principles enshrined in it—the principles of a state based on the rule of law, of equal rights, of social justice. In this historic hour, we German Social Democrats solemnly pledge ourselves to the principles of humanity and justice, of freedom and socialism. No Enabling Act gives you the power to destroy ideas that are eternal and indestructible."
- Otto Wels, Speech Against the Passage of the Enabling Act, 1933

<img src="img/reichstag_3.jpg" alt="The Reichstag Interior">

It is a grim time for German democracy. Following the largest crash in the stock market the world has seen, a worldwide depression has started, hitting Germany especially hard. The Nazis are ascendant and our support is dwindling as our coalition nears collapse.

It will be our responsibility to ensure that this crisis of capitalism will not end so badly for the working class.

Please select your desired difficulty to begin.

- @1930_easy: Begin (easy difficulty)
- @1930_main: Begin (normal difficulty)
- @1930_hard: Begin (hard difficulty)
- @1930_historical: Begin (historical mode)
- @1925_start: Change to 1925 Start Date
- @1928_start: Change to 1928 Start Date
- @settings: Settings.

@1928_easy
view-if: year == 1928
on-arrival: difficulty = -1; resources = 4; dues = 3; rb_strength = 2500; uspd_relation = 29; z_relation = 54; dvp_relation = 49; budget = 5;
go-to: 1928_main

@1928_hard
view-if: year == 1928
on-arrival: difficulty = 1; resources = 0; dues = 1; rb_strength = 1000; reformist_dissent = 25; left_dissent = 30; labor_dissent = 25; center_dissent = 25; z_relation = 41; uspd_relation = 16; dvp_relation = 31; budget = 3;
go-to: 1928_main

@1928_historical
view-if: year == 1928
subtitle: Saving, loading, and polls will be disabled. [? if not achievement_game_completed: Not recommended for a first playthrough. ?]
on-arrival: {!
Q.difficulty = 2;
Q.historical_mode = 1;
Q.resources = 2;
Q.dues = 1;
Q.rb_strength = 2000;
Q.reformist_dissent = 25;
Q.left_dissent = 30;
Q.labor_dissent = 25;
Q.center_dissent = 25;
Q.z_relation = 41;
Q.uspd_relation = 16;
Q.dvp_relation = 31;
Q.budget = 2;
this.state.disableSaves = true;
!}
go-to: 1928_main

@1930_easy
view-if: year == 1930
on-arrival: difficulty = -1; resources = 4; dues = 3; rb_strength = 2500; uspd_relation += 9; z_relation += 5; dvp_relation += 9; budget += 1
go-to: 1930_main

